{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940193-merits-and-flaws-from-other-cwod-books","id":940193,"title":"Merits and Flaws from other cWoD books.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-30T12:35:02-07:00","id":940193,"title":"Merits and Flaws from other cWoD books.","content":"The title explains it all, I'm wondering in case the Storyteller can allow merits from other books to be used in the game; for example. I've been roleplaying a Demon following Demon: the Fallen setting, during character creation, I've found a merit called &quot;Fast Learner&quot; in the demon book, I wasn't really satisified with it, since there's another merit with exactly the same effect if not better. I saw no point in picking it, however. A few days prior to that, I've been reading Changeling: the Dreaming player handguide and found a pretty neat Merit with the same title, which allows the character to recieve an extra +1 Experience Point at the end of each story. It's not really that much, but it does give a better effect than the Demon version of the Merit, the storyteller had doubts about allowing it, so he told me to ask here if it would be allowed to use it.<br /> The Merits are:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon the Fallen player handguide</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Fast Learner (3 pt. Merit)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">You learn the basics of a subject very quickly indeed. The first dot of an Ability costs 1 XP, rather then three. Other levels cost the regular amount.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\">\u25cf Fast Learner (3pt. Merit, Changeling: Second Edition, p. 158) You learn very quickly, and pick up on new things faster than most do. You gain one extra experience point at the conclusion of each story (not each game session).</span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T14:06:11-07:00","id":940245,"title":"","content":"I usually allow any merits/flaws from other games as long as they don't rely on being splat-specific. Mind you, this is as long as it makes sense for the character.<br /> <br /> With the Merits above, I don't see the big deal. Neither is game breaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T16:12:10-07:00","id":940318,"title":"","content":"I generally give my players a list of allowed Backgrounds, Merits, and Flaws that are from multiple sources. Some, like Ability Aptitude and Legendary Attribute are quite fun when combined with Vampire and Werewolf games, so I let people take them in every game. Others, like most of the Merits from Hunter and Demon, are too weak to have players take by mistake because I do not want to hear them complain about it five sessions on. <br /> <br /> I also change Merits. Natural Linguist, for example, increases Linguistics by three, to a maximum effective level of eight, only for the purposes of determining the number of languages known to the character because +3 dice to every die roll involving languages, written or spoken, is far too powerful for 2 points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T17:52:44-07:00","id":940361,"title":"","content":"I see. Thanks for your answers guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T23:18:04-07:00","id":940502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940193-merits-and-flaws-from-other-cwod-books?p=940318#post940318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally give my players a list of allowed Backgrounds, Merits, and Flaws that are from multiple sources. Some, like Ability Aptitude and Legendary Attribute are quite fun when combined with Vampire and Werewolf games, so I let people take them in every game. Others, like most of the Merits from Hunter and Demon, are too weak to have players take by mistake because I do not want to hear them complain about it five sessions on.<br /> <br /> I also change Merits. Natural Linguist, for example, increases Linguistics by three, to a maximum effective level of eight, only for the purposes of determining the number of languages known to the character because +3 dice to every die roll involving languages, written or spoken, is far too powerful for 2 points.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am the same. I write up a list of all M&amp;F and from what book that can be taken. HOWEVER, if there is a merit/flaw for YOUR group, and there is other ones called the same in other books, whether better/worse or less/more costly(freebie granting), IMC you have to take YOUR books one..<br /> So in that demon case above, even though the Fast learner is in other sources, a Demon PC has to use the one in his guide..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T23:23:05-07:00","id":940506,"title":"","content":"Hm, does anyone else think that Natural Linguist is phenomenally overpowered for its price? A +3 die pool bonus to any use of language, write or spoken, for only 2 bonus points? How many abilities does that include?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T06:41:59-07:00","id":940602,"title":"","content":"But linguistics as an ability always worked differently than other abilities. It was supposed to be used for languages known. I'm not sure which edition book this writing of the merit came from. In early editions that would just mean the person knew 3 additional languages. Later editions would've been more complicated since each dot doubled the number of languages you knew. In any case, I always read Linguistics as being purely the number of languages you could speak, not as a dice pool you rolled generally to speak.<br /> Makes some sense in the 20th anniversary books that they moved the entire knowledge to being a merit. Personally I prefer to move the language knowledge as it was written in revised to being a background instead. Languages as backgrounds make more sense to me than as Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T11:49:04-07:00","id":940731,"title":"","content":"But the Merit is still overpowered in V20. You gain +3 dice for any use of language, spoken or written, as well as doubling the number of language gained from purchasing the Language Merit. The bonus from Natural Linguist could easily apply to every mundane use of six Abilities: Expression, Intimidation, Leadership, Etiquette, Performance, and Politics. Heck, I would think that every character (especially vampires) with any pretensions towards a social life should take the Merit of Natural Linguist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:21:43-07:00","id":940744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940193-merits-and-flaws-from-other-cwod-books?p=940731#post940731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Merit is still overpowered in V20. You gain +3 dice for any use of language, spoken or written, as well as doubling the number of language gained from purchasing the Language Merit. The bonus from Natural Linguist could easily apply to every mundane use of six Abilities: Expression, Intimidation, Leadership, Etiquette, Performance, and Politics. Heck, I would think that every character (especially vampires) with any pretensions towards a social life should take the Merit of Natural Linguist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think those bonus dice applying to all of those skills is a very liberal (and wrong imo) interpretation of the text. It is 3 additional dice that apply to <i>just</i> languages. There are very few rolls that this is going to apply to. Need to decipher something? Then maybe. Convincing someone of something? Just no.<br /> Reading it over a few times, it in no way seems overpowered to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:37:48-07:00","id":940753,"title":"","content":"It says specifically 'You have a flair for languages. You may add three dice to <i>any </i>dice pool involving written or spoken languages.' If nothing else, it needs an errata because it does not say anything about deciphering or interpreting languages, it says <i>any </i>dice pool involving written or spoken languages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:37:57-07:00","id":940960,"title":"","content":"Oh Curious? <br /> <br /> Whats a good Flaw to take to Reflect that &quot;your&quot; Resources rating derives from a kinfolk,ghoul etc, who is hosting you indefinitely, <br /> <br /> I think a Camarilla vampire, especialy a ventrue, would likely feel somewhat beholden to his host.<br /> <br /> Most Garou may view kin as inferior but still view them as family, and will see being too demanding as something meriting a lecture beating... or worse.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:57:56-07:00","id":940967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940193-merits-and-flaws-from-other-cwod-books?p=940960#post940960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh Curious?<br /> <br /> Whats a good Flaw to take to Reflect that &quot;your&quot; Resources rating derives from a kinfolk,ghoul etc, who is hosting you indefinitely,<br /> <br /> I think a Camarilla vampire, especialy a ventrue, would likely feel somewhat beholden to his host.<br /> <br /> Most Garou may view kin as inferior but still view them as family, and will see being too demanding as something meriting a lecture beating... or worse.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there needs to be a flaw. Where your resources come from is part of the character background. If its from retainers or kinfolk, that is built in. The negative aspect to that is that if something happens to said person, you can possibly lose 2 different backgrounds.<br /> And this might just be my games, but Garou do not give out &quot;lecture beatings&quot; to Kinfolk. There can certainly be individual, but in general you don't treat family like that. Or do you mean that <i>other</i> Garou would give a Garou dependent on Kinfolk for money these beatings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T18:03:23-07:00","id":940970,"title":"","content":"that they'd give a garou who was seen as &quot;too demanding&quot; In their judgement of his kinfolk those beatings","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T21:38:28-07:00","id":941028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940193-merits-and-flaws-from-other-cwod-books?p=940960#post940960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh Curious?<br /> <br /> Whats a good Flaw to take to Reflect that &quot;your&quot; Resources rating derives from a kinfolk,ghoul etc, who is hosting you indefinitely,<br /> <br /> I think a Camarilla vampire, especialy a ventrue, would likely feel somewhat beholden to his host.<br /> <br /> Most Garou may view kin as inferior but still view them as family, and will see being too demanding as something meriting a lecture beating... or worse.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe something like ward, but rather than YOU having to care for the person, THEY care for you...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T02:04:41-07:00","id":941104,"title":"","content":"Not sure where it is from, but I usually like &quot;Charmed Existence (5pt. Merit)&quot; it is a solely mechanical merit. It allows for one '1' to be ignored per roll, slightly increasing the number of successes and massively reducing the chance of a botch on every roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T00:20:16-07:00","id":942547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940193-merits-and-flaws-from-other-cwod-books?p=941104#post941104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure where it is from, but I usually like &amp;quot;Charmed Existence (5pt. Merit)&amp;quot; it is a solely mechanical merit. It allows for one '1' to be ignored per roll, slightly increasing the number of successes and massively reducing the chance of a botch on every roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Combine with daredevil and self-confident for truly astounding (albeit a little cheesy) effects","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:49:24-07:00","id":943231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/940193-merits-and-flaws-from-other-cwod-books?p=942547#post942547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Combine with daredevil and self-confident for truly astounding (albeit a little cheesy) effects</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen someone do the daredevil/self confident or Charmed+self confident thing before.. Never all 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T23:25:20-07:00","id":943438,"title":"","content":"Together the three weigh in for 13 points...<br /> <br /> <br /> Charmed + confident for 10 Freebies is costly enough.<br /> <br /> If you can afford only one, then the charmed existence is best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":". 08-04-2016, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T10:44:02-07:00","id":943705,"title":"","content":"This is where Dhamyr, with their Joss Pool and 25 freebie points, really start to shine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr